  "response_to_critic": "Revised milestone to use the supported rule type 'position_near_with_facing' instead of the unsupported 'position_near', 'facing_block', and OR/AND nesting. The new rule targets the closest dead bush at (3,0,3) spawn-relative with max_distance=5 (player must be within 5 blocks) and facing_tolerance=60 degrees (player must be looking toward it). I chose max_distance=5 rather than 16 because the dead bush is only ~4.2 blocks from spawn — a distance of 5 ensures the player has actually navigated toward it rather than just looking from spawn. Since there are 4 dead bushes in the scene and the evaluator only supports flat rule arrays (no OR logic), I target the closest one which the preview confirmed the agent naturally approaches.",
